`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Isolation and entrypoints:"})," Generation receives task documents without benchmark tests. Separate evaluation mounts the submission and checker inputs read-only and writes reports separately. ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"docker_run.sh"})," supports Claude Code/Codex generation; ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"docker_test.sh"})," evaluates an existing HTML without a model key. Isolation reduces experiment-time exposure but does not establish training-data decontamination. ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/blob/6427cb6517ce11ff350ec45fcae17b67c5aec245/docker_test.sh",children:"Evaluation orchestration"}),", ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/blob/6427cb6517ce11ff350ec45fcae17b67c5aec245/docker_test_entrypoint.sh",children:"entrypoint"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Metric boundary:"})," The report's strict success requires recorded successful generation, usable evaluation results, every L1 check passing, and applicable checks in ",e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"both P0 and P1"}),", all passing; P2 is excluded. Its denominator is ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"len(results)"}),": the stock collector includes every task directory, even those with missing summaries. Test-only submissions contribute check pass rates but not strict successes; generation metadata is not independent authentication. The paper's 26/47 best strict result belongs to its reported experiment, not this audit. ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/blob/6427cb6517ce11ff350ec45fcae17b67c5aec245/scripts/gen_report.py",children:"Report implementation"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Availability and limits:"})," The repository is ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/blob/6427cb6517ce11ff350ec45fcae17b67c5aec245/LICENSE",children:"Apache-2.0"}),"; third-party materials retain their own terms. The paper describes verified reference implementations, but the ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://api.github.com/repos/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/git/trees/6c9c4e334bd166e924ed430f567ec78cb77feb9a?recursive=1",children:"complete pinned release tree"})," contains no HTML files, so do not describe reference games or generated HTML as released by this tree. The ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/areal-project/GameASG-Bench/blob/6427cb6517ce11ff350ec45fcae17b67c5aec245/Dockerfile",children:"Dockerfile"})," pins agent CLI versions but not the base-image digest, apt/Chromium packages or ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"ws"}),"; record those before reproduction. The sampled TDD also mentions ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"design-doc.md"}),", absent from that task's three-file release, a documentation inconsistency rather than an established runtime blocker."]}),`
