`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Task boundary:"})," The paper evaluates autonomous bug discovery in 30 game environments containing 124 human-verified defects, not production of a new game or successful repair. Agents interact through backend APIs; exploration-only and specification/source-informed conditions are separate. A critic matches reported defects to annotations to compute recall. This does not establish visual QA, false-positive control or generated-game quality. ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.02648v1",children:"Paper §§3–5"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Historical artifact boundary:"})," The March 29 snapshot includes the agent, prompts, evaluator and one Dark Castle environment with ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/camel-ai/GBQA/blob/ca7e3fb652a2e4826d0f14392a9a390522a1f1a7/hub/dark-castle/bugs/dark-castle.json",children:"three annotated bugs"}),". Its ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://api.github.com/repos/camel-ai/GBQA/git/trees/ca7e3fb652a2e4826d0f14392a9a390522a1f1a7?recursive=1",children:"complete tree"})," does not contain the reported 30-game corpus or a LICENSE file. This is an inspectable paper-era example, not a verified paper release or a claim about every historical revision."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Later protocol boundary:"})," At June 25 revision ",e.jsx(a.code,{children:"500e5ea"}),", the ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/camel-ai/GBQA/blob/500e5ea252ee7afccc275b0e28fbd6de8c8f5dfc/README.md",children:"README"})," describes a broader software-QA framework with a selected bug hint and a binary reward for a complete report whose source pinpoint aligns with a golden patch. Its ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://api.github.com/repos/camel-ai/GBQA/git/trees/500e5ea252ee7afccc275b0e28fbd6de8c8f5dfc?recursive=1",children:"tree"})," has three named Dark Castle target-task packages plus a template, not three distinct games. The ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/camel-ai/GBQA/blob/500e5ea252ee7afccc275b0e28fbd6de8c8f5dfc/gbqa/tasks/dark-castle-key-fragment-combine/gbqa.yaml",children:"key-fragment manifest"})," specifies medium hinting, a separate upstream release and Daytona/Modal execution. These are not the paper's recall protocol; patch-shaped localization evidence is not proof of a repaired game. Runtime and verifier behavior were not independently tested."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.li,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Reuse boundary:"})," The later revision has an ",e.jsx(a.a,{href:"https://github.com/camel-ai/GBQA/blob/500e5ea252ee7afccc275b0e28fbd6de8c8f5dfc/LICENSE",children:"Apache-2.0 LICENSE"}),". That observation does not establish rights for missing corpus content or separately fetched software/assets. Full paper-corpus reproduction remains unverified: obtain the designated revision, environment/annotation inventory and matching evaluation configuration before comparing results."]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.p,{children:[e.jsx(a.strong,{children:"Editorial use:"})," Record whether a QA task is open-ended discovery or hinted diagnosis, whether source code is visible, and whether the score measures defect recall, localization or actual repair. Keep these outcomes separate from game-generation acceptance. Neither an author-linked repository nor a historical commit alone establishes release completeness."]}),`
