`,e.jsx(a.p,{children:"Integrate these as a focused evaluation-methods note before adding broad catalog entries. OpenGameEval and GameASG-Bench have inspected code/task surfaces with distinct hosted-service, reference-artifact and dependency limitations; the remaining studies warrant explicit paper/protocol or partial-artifact labels until their executable releases are established. Neither inspected release is a fully reproduced benchmark. GBQA adds inspectable historical/current QA examples without establishing its complete paper corpus. Five useful distinctions emerge:"}),`
`,e.jsxs(a.ol,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(a.li,{children:"Engine-state checks and visual judgment answer different questions."}),`
